{"title":"2005 IMO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Determine all positive integers relatively prime to all the terms of the infinite sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/f/a3f3c15ee9d92c2eb2747f800d908cfa7aa6a08b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_n=2^n+3^n+6^n -1,\\ n\\geq 1.\\]\" width=\"234\" height=\"16\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-rRPkQrmzJw\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-rRPkQrmzJw</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> be a positive integer that satisfies the given condition.\n</p><p>For all primes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/4/4843d240c7b2c54b45cfc9ed28b13887dfd36adb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p&gt;3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />, by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Fermat%27s_Little_Theorem\" title=\"Fermat&#39;s Little Theorem\">Fermat's Little Theorem</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/0/7e00b36dda614729213a8681dc749f15585ca078.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^{p-1} \\equiv 1\\pmod p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"143\" height=\"21\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are relatively prime. This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1c96c14239af78e5cf52bbe5ed3edc91a28187.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^{p-3} \\equiv \\frac{1}{n^2} \\pmod p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"156\" height=\"38\" />. Plugging <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/4/544fe8ae05957e3e729a7c2e678e67951aa55148.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = p-3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"17\" /> back into the equation, we see that the value<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/9/0f965eb9407014fe0e4fc671eed0acbfd84eddb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mod p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" /> is simply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/6/556e8dd3425dad11dacdc6aa7ac4ea3e19bda148.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{9} + \\frac{3}{4} + \\frac{1}{36} - 1 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"159\" height=\"38\" />. Thus, the expression is divisible by all primes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/5/2d5ea01976f8b068727b59cdf4c294ac323784aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p&gt;3.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"17\" /> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/3/cf3faada90ada2470dd30a5bcf8d7baf222c0945.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2 = 48 = 2^4 \\cdot 3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"129\" height=\"20\" /> we can conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> cannot have any prime divisors. Therefore, our answer is only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/d/6cdd1b53e5faf7a118222e4b7571d1e9afa0cf56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO\" title=\"2005 IMO\">2005 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2005 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2005 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2005 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2005 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2005 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2005 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2005 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2005 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017205616\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.018 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.023 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 109/1000000\nPost